/*
 * Declares the set of native types. Types that are built into the Ymir language
 * itself.
 *
 * Native types include primitive scalars(integers, floats, characters),
 * built-in function and delegate types, the `void` and `none` markers, and
 * other fundamental types required by the language runtime.
 *
 * These types are defined directly by the compiler and do not originate from
 * user code. They form the foundation upon which all higher-level types are
 * constructed.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::type::native
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/type/native.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
